I have a version of NetHack 3.0 patchlevel 6, overlayed PC version with
all options enabled.  I played with the makefile and the code a bit and
now it runs great on a 8MHz 286 with 640K.  It is available for anonymous
FTP from psuvm.psu.edu.

Unfortunatly this version will only run on a 286 or 386 (no XTs).  If and
when I get a 8088 version working I will post that it is available.

Nethack is split up into two ZOOed files.  Zoo is available from many places.
Note that psuvm is a IBM CMS system and FTP is a little bit different than
usual in that you have to specify what disk you want to use:

action                                           command
------------------------------------------------------------------
ftp to psuvm.psu.edu  (128.118.56.2)             ftp psuvm.psu.edu
log on with any userid and any password.
change to kqs's 102 disk                         cd kqs.102
set file type to binary                          binary
get nh306exe.zoo and nh306sup.zoo                get nh306exe.zoo
                                                 get nh306sup.zoo
leave ftp                                        quit

